<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION RISES LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION RISES LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The total capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse rose to 8.2 billion litas last week from 8.1</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the bourse told Reuters that the exchange</p>
<p>was now calculating total market capitalisation, including the</p>
<p>secondary T-bill market.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					    July 21-25     July 14-18</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  16,289	   15,495</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   918		909</p>
<p>    Number of transactions on     655		717</p>
<p>Central market (CM)</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     18.015 mln     25.14 mln</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 133		97</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   6.217 mln	25.888 mln</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     60.22 mln	52.855 mln</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     6.571 mln	8.077 mln</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   8		  20</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	15.245	    21.575</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
